From: Stanislaw Pal <kuncy7@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: ipq5018: let the CPU boost to 1296 MHz

With the PLL change parked on GPLL0 (0973), the CPU can move between
operating points. Add 1296 MHz above the rated 1008 MHz, so that
schedutil raises the clock under load and drops back to 1008 MHz
otherwise. Both come from the PLL (L = 42 and 54 of the 24 MHz XO): the
mux driver puts the CPU back on the PLL after every rate change, so an
operating point served by GPLL0, such as the 800 MHz one 0912 removed,
would leave the clock framework and the hardware disagreeing.

The boards have no CPU regulator, so the voltage stays at 1.1 V at both
rates. That is also why there is no operating point below 1008 MHz: at
a fixed voltage it would save little, and idle cores sit in WFI anyway.
The cpu-thermal passive trip at 100 C throttles through cpufreq.

Signed-off-by: Stanislaw Pal <kuncy7@gmail.com>
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/ipq5018.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/ipq5018.dtsi
@@ -100,6 +100,12 @@
 			opp-microvolt = <1100000>;
 			clock-latency-ns = <200000>;
 		};
+
+		opp-1296000000 {
+			opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <1296000000>;
+			opp-microvolt = <1100000>;
+			clock-latency-ns = <200000>;
+		};
 	};
 
 	firmware {
